


---

In a small, colorful town, where every house had tiny gardens filled with flowers, a little boy named Arjun sat on the roof, staring at the sky. He held a small telescope in his hands and smiled as he counted the stars. He thought, “I should do something new today… maybe I can surprise my friend Riya.”

He went down the stairs and walked through the narrow street, and there he saw Riya playing with her dog, Bruno, in her garden. “Riya! Look at me! Look at me!” Arjun shouted. Riya looked up, laughing, “Arjun! Did you bring another one of your crazy ideas again?”

Arjun pulled a small cardboard rocket from his pocket and showed it to her. “Look! I designed this rocket! Today, we’re going to have a little race to see which rocket can reach the sky!” Riya rolled her eyes and laughed. “Arjun, you always get lost in your imagination. Okay, let’s see if it actually works.”

They placed the rocket in an open area of the garden and pushed it gently. The rocket slowly went up, but suddenly a strong gust of wind blew it into the pond. Bruno, who was always adventurous, ran to the pond and nudged the rocket back to Arjun and Riya with his little nose. “Thanks, Bruno! You’re a real hero! Riya, next time we’ll make the rocket even stronger,” Arjun said. Riya smiled, “Yes, and this time we’ll plan it carefully, like real scientists.”

They decided to go to the town park and organize a bigger rocket race with all the kids. When they arrived at the park, they saw other children there too, each with colorful rockets of different designs. Everyone was excited. Arjun and Riya formed their team, and the rocket launches began. All the rockets flew up into the sky, but suddenly, Arjun’s rocket got stuck in a tree. “Oh no! What do we do now?” Riya asked. Arjun thought for a moment and said, “Hmm… let’s use a rope and pulley.” He carefully retrieved the rocket from the tree using the rope. All the kids were impressed with Arjun’s clever idea.

The race ended, and all the rockets landed safely. Arjun and Riya saw that their rocket came in second place, but it didn’t matter. The most fun they had was solving problems together and using their imagination. As the sun began to set, Arjun and Riya sat on a park bench looking at the sky. “Riya, today was amazing. The rocket race, Bruno’s heroics, and our teamwork… it was all perfect,” Arjun said. Riya held his hand and said, “Yes, and this is just the beginning. Tomorrow, new adventures are waiting for us.” Bruno raised his little paw as if to high-five them, then happily trotted home with them through the garden path. Stars twinkled in the sky, and Arjun thought, “Nothing is bigger than imagination and friendship. Tomorrow we’ll have more fun with new rockets and new adventures.” And so, another memorable day of adventure ended for Arjun, Riya, and Bruno, but their excitement and curiosity stayed alive.


